  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "The native adapter emits mirrored parent-local bounds and visibility with floating-point physical scroll offsets. Rust normalizes offsets, accumulates hierarchy coordinates and returns visible nodes with inherited clip rectangles.",
    "Offscreen rejection happens in Rust before row title/color preparation. Invisible native subtrees remain shallow placeholders to avoid scanning inactive workspace caches.",
    "The Rust viewport retains an ancestry scratch buffer across updates. Intermediate coordinates use f64; invalid dimensions, non-finite inputs and forward/invalid parent indices are rejected safely.",
    "Card/text bounds stay untrimmed at the viewport edge. Every emitted primitive carries its item clip, which Metal applies as a rounded-out, drawable-bounded device-pixel scissor. Identical consecutive scissor rectangles reuse encoder state.",
    "The native browser regression compares a card at y=-9.25 and its 24.75-high visible clip with native floating-point geometry and the last submitted primitive signature. The visible fragment hits the real native row.",
    "The same regression requests a programmatic y offset of 1000000 and verifies that Rust normalizes the physical adapter to its maximum offset, then checks the last real row geometry/clip.",
    "Rust unit tests cover fractional projection, inherited parent clipping/visibility, content shrink, offset bounds, invalid geometry and propagation of clips into every draw primitive.",
    "Existing native wheel/physical mouse-after-scroll, drag/close, split and pin/folder placement, tree state, warm-sidebars, scene text, fallback animation, sessions, palettes and settings regressions pass."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The signed isolated app displayed the original Unicode split pair and indented pin/folder rows.",
    "Scrolling the sidebar down revealed tabs 8 through 24; the native scrollbar stayed visible outside the Metal canvas and rows remained confined to the list viewport.",
    "Selecting tab 24 opened its real page. Scrolling back up restored the folder and split pair; selecting the first pair member restored the original split view.",
    "The demo retains its 24 work tabs, expanded folder and original pair. The prototype was closed; the normal app/profile was not used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native View containers, measurement/local bounds, mirrored geometry and physical wheel/trackpad/scrollbar adapters remain. This does not remove the native scroll hierarchy.",
    "Fractional bounds/clip assertions inspect submitted display-list metadata. Device-pixel scissor edges are rounded out; there is no pixel-golden comparison at every scale or real-trackpad timing capture in this run.",
    "Submitted command buffers and functional elapsed times are not GPU completion or physical presentation measurements. No end-to-end performance gain is asserted.",
    "Native animation snapshots, outer sidebar controls, split headers/divider, palettes/forms and full IME/VoiceOver/non-macOS coverage remain migration work.",
    "No new third-party crate, library or binary framework was added."
  ]
